  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1030 PM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nOn Thursday, the remains of Edouard should be found wobbling \naround central or northern Texas while we hold onto a fraction of \nmonsoonal moisture largely anchored over southern AZ and NM. This \nmoist plume should aid in another round of very spotty afternoon \nshowers/storms across our far W-NW zones. High temps should reach\ntheir hottest readings for the week on Thursday before thicknesses\ndecline thereafter accompanying deeper ESE flow thanks to the \nupper high retreating and staying just north of I40. Ensemble \nspread grows this weekend into next week regarding this high's \nposition and strength, yet it remains close enough to us to keep \na lid on additional precip chances.",
